course: dictionary
lesson: 2525
title: Breaking things down
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words name a process, a thing that happens step by step. Decomposition is one of these. «Worms, fungi and bacteria break down dead plants and animals into soil; this is called decomposition.» So decomposition is the name for that slow breaking down.
explain: The same word is used in maths. Splitting 47 into 40 + 7 is number decomposition, because you break one number into smaller parts. Breaking a shape into rectangles to find its area is also decomposition.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. The words break down and into soil tell you the big thing becomes smaller, simpler things. When you meet decomposition, ask: what is being broken into what?
fact: Decomposition means the natural breaking down of dead plants and animals into simpler things.
fact: The decomposers are bacteria, fungi and worms. They do the breaking down.
fact: Decomposition returns nutrients to the soil, so new plants can grow.
fact: In maths, decomposition means breaking a number or shape into smaller parts, such as 47 = 40 + 7.
fact: In chemistry, decomposition is when a substance breaks into simpler substances by a chemical reaction.
exercise: «Worms, fungi and bacteria break down dead plants and animals into soil; this is called decomposition.» What is decomposition? | *The natural breaking down of dead plants and animals into simpler things | A way of counting big numbers | The growing of new plants in spring | Digging holes for worms
exercise: Splitting 47 into 40 + 7 is an example of what? | Multiplication | *Number decomposition | Rounding | Measuring
exercise: Ben says decomposition means a tidy bedroom. What does it really mean? | Painting walls in bright colours | A tidy place to keep books | *The breaking down of dead things into simpler things | Making a bedroom bigger
test: Fungi are decomposers. What do they do to dead plants? | Freeze them solid | *Break them down into simpler things | Make them grow taller | Paint them
test: In chemistry, decomposition means a substance breaks into what? | Water only | Bigger, heavier substances | Nothing at all | *Simpler substances, by a chemical reaction
exam: Why does decomposition matter for a garden? | It makes the soil freeze | *It turns dead plants into simpler things that feed the soil | It only happens in deserts | It stops plants from ever growing
